    <dcterms:title>Sybil, Or, The Two Nations</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sybil_(novel)</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>Produced by David G. Johnson, and David Widger</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"Sybil, Or, The Two Nations by Earl of Beaconsfield Benjamin Disraeli" is a novel published in 1845. This work examines the desperate conditions of England's working classes during the industrial age. Inspired by the Chartist movement and a government inquiry into child labor, Disraeli crafted a story that exposes the moral corruption of forcing children into harsh employment. The novel traces the struggles of workers living in squalor, creating a passionate argument for social reform in a deeply divided England. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 68.0 (8th &amp; 9th grade). Neither easy nor difficult to read.</pgterms:marc908>
